Memo

To:

Honorable City Council
From:
Brian N. Kozak, Chief of Police
Date:
May 8, 2013
Re:

Alarm Ordinance Revision Staff Report

Summary:

The Police Department recommends amendments to the alarm ordinance (Chapter 8.08) to
add requirements for call verification, graduated fees for false alarms and ability to suspend
a permit when the alarm has been designated as unreliable.  The revisions will reduce false
alarms, making police service more efficient and cost effective for the citizens of Cheyenne.

Background:

In 2012 the Cheyenne Police Department responded to 1,863 alarm calls, which had the
following dispositions:

False alarms

1,442
Canceled after dispatched

352
Canceled prior to dispatch

